an5.40:3.1 starts: so, when the head of a family here
an5.40:3.2 starts: possesses faith and virtue,
an5.40:3.3 starts: his wife, children, and relatives
an5.40:3.4 starts: all grow in dependence on him;
an5.40:3.5 starts: so too his companions, his family circle,
an5.40:3.6 starts: and those dependent on him.
an5.40:4.1 starts: Those possessed of discernment,
an5.40:4.2 starts: seeing that virtuous man’s good conduct,
an5.40:4.3 starts: his generosity and good deeds,
an5.40:4.4 starts: emulate his example.
an5.40:5.1 starts: Having lived here in accord with Dhamma,
an5.40:5.2 starts: the path leading to a good destination,
an5.40:5.3 starts: those who desire sensual pleasures rejoice,
an5.40:5.4 starts: delighting in the deva world.
an5.42:3.1 starts: The deities protect one guarded by the Dhamma,
an5.42:3.2 starts: who has managed his wealth for the welfare
an5.42:3.3 starts: Fame does not forsake one steadfast in the
an5.42:3.4 starts: who is learned and of virtuous behavior and
an5.43:9.1 starts: For one desiring long life, beauty, fame,
an5.43:9.2 starts: acclaim, heaven, high families,
an5.43:9.3 starts: and lofty delights
an5.43:9.4 starts: following in succession,
an5.45:7.1 starts: Just as the many rivers used by the
an5.45:7.2 starts: flowing downstream, reach the ocean,
an5.45:7.3 starts: the great mass of water, the boundless sea,
an5.45:7.4 starts: the fearsome receptacle of heaps of gems;
an5.45:8.1 starts: so the streams of merit reach the wise
an5.45:8.2 starts: who is a giver of food, drink, and
an5.45:8.3 starts: they reach the donor of beds, seats, and
an5.45:8.4 starts: like rivers carrying their waters to the sea.
an5.47:9.1 starts: Therefore an intelligent person,
an5.47:9.2 starts: remembering the Buddhas’ teaching,
an5.47:9.3 starts: should be intent on faith and virtuous behavior,
an5.47:9.4 starts: confidence and vision of the Dhamma.
an5.55:10.1 starts: But those who have fully understood sense pleasures
an5.55:10.2 starts: live without fear from any quarter.
an5.55:10.3 starts: Having attained the destruction of the taints,
an5.55:10.4 starts: while in the world, they have gone beyond.
an5.57:16.1 starts: Now I am incapable
an5.57:16.2 starts: of indulging in sensual pleasures.
an5.57:16.3 starts: Relying on the spiritual life,
an5.57:16.4 starts: never will I turn back.”
an8.29:13.1 starts: If one has directly encountered them,
an8.29:13.2 starts: fortune rarely gained in the world,
an8.29:13.3 starts: if one has obtained the human state,
an8.29:13.4 starts: and the good Dhamma is being taught,
an8.29:13.5 starts: for a person desiring his own good,
an8.29:13.6 starts: this is incentive enough to strive.
